## CoalesceBatchesExec with fetch
    CoalesceBatchesExec: target_batch_size=8192, fetch=10
      MockSourceExec: partitioning=UnknownPartitioning(3), partition_rows=[100, 200, 300], statistics=Exact
[invariant] A2 fetch_not_equal_cardinality at CoalesceBatchesExec (root): fetch() is Some(10), but cardinality_effect() is Equal; a fetch can drop input rows, so the effect should be LowerEqual while a fetch is set
[invariant] A8 partition_statistics_sum at CoalesceBatchesExec (root): overall num_rows is Exact(10), but the exact per-partition num_rows [10, 10, 10] sum to 30
[invariant] B2 exact_statistics_hold at CoalesceBatchesExec (root): overall statistics report num_rows Exact(10), but the output has Exact(30) rows
[invariant] B8 cardinality_effect_holds at CoalesceBatchesExec (root): cardinality_effect() is Equal, but the node produced 30 rows from 600 input rows
[lint] B10 boundedness_holds at CoalesceBatchesExec (root): rebuilt with child 0 unbounded, the node reports Boundedness::Unbounded, but it has fetch Some(10) and otherwise passes every row through, so like GlobalLimitExec its output ends once the fetch is reached

